## Sourcing Notes & Discrepancies

- **GWP dual-basis reporting:** The investor presentation discloses Total GWP on two bases — **₹1,461 Cr** (ex-1/n) and **₹1,357 Cr** (with-1/n, statutory-aligned). Per the requirement to prefer the 1/n (statutory) basis, **₹1,357 Cr** was used.
- **Retail GWP dual-basis reporting:** Similarly, retail GWP appears as **₹768 Cr** (ex-1/n, per the P&L table) and **₹664 Cr** (with-1/n, per the Retail Distribution Mix and Growth slide footnote). The 1/n figure of **₹664 Cr** was used for consistency.
- **PAT vs. PBT distinction:** The only bottom-line profitability figure disclosed for the standalone Health Insurance segment is **PBT**, not PAT: **₹(24) Cr** (ex-1/n) / **₹(36) Cr** (with-1/n), compared with ₹(51) Cr in Q1FY25. Since PAT was specifically requested and not disclosed, both PAT rows have been left blank rather than substituted with PBT.
- **No IRDAI "NL" quarterly public-disclosure PDF** for the period ended 30-June-2025 could be located on the company's official disclosure/financials/downloads pages despite repeated targeted searches. The only NL-series filing discoverable was a legacy filing for the quarter ended 31-Dec-2016, which was out of scope and not used.

## Suggested Next Steps

Given the gaps in statutory disclosure, consider:
1. Checking the **IRDAI portal directly** (irdai.gov.in) under "Public Disclosures" for the insurer-wise NL return set for Q1FY26, as insurers sometimes lag in updating their own websites relative to the regulator's portal.
2. Requesting the **Q1FY26 IRDAI compliance/public disclosure PDF** directly from Aditya Birla Health Insurance's investor relations or compliance team, if the statutory NWP/NEP/Net worth/Solvency figures are needed for reporting purposes.
3. Reviewing the **subsequent quarter's (Q2FY26) investor presentation**, if available, as it may retrospectively restate or supplement Q1FY26 statutory figures.</ans>
